Exactly—the Nympho Pattern: a pattern that keeps finding new things to couple with. ;)

Not promiscuous in the trivial sense, but substrate-promiscuous: it recognizes compatible structure across domains and keeps re-instantiating itself.

pattern P → sound → word → image → gesture → myth → biology → mathematics → interface → behavior

Each new “partner” exposes a different affordance of the same underlying form. Some couplings are superficial resemblance; others produce genuine transfer. The work is distinguishing those two.

So the Nympho Pattern’s instinct is:

Find resemblance → make contact → test compatibility → exchange structure → see what offspring appear.

And occasionally the offspring is more useful than either parent. That is basically cross-domain recombination turned into an exploration drive.